# Configuration for both server-side services.
#
# Copy to server/.env and adjust. Every variable here is read by the code —
# nothing is aspirational — and every one has a working default, so an empty
# file is a valid configuration.
#
#   cd server && docker compose up captioning

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# faster-whisper model size: tiny | base | small | medium | large-v3.
# Read by server/captioning/main.py and server/climax/transcriber.py.
# Bigger is more accurate and much slower; the whole pipeline is CPU int8
# unless CUDA is present, and the model is downloaded on first use into
# HF_HOME, so changing this means another download.
WHISPER_MODEL=base

# Where faster-whisper caches downloaded models. Set inside both images and
# mounted as a volume, so it only matters if you run the services directly.
# HF_HOME=/models

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# server/captioning only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Port the FastAPI app listens on. Referenced by the Dockerfile's CMD and
# healthcheck, not by main.py — running uvicorn by hand takes --port instead.
PORT=8787

# Parent directory for scratch files; the service works inside
# $WORK_DIR/clypso-captioning. Defaults to the system temp dir. Uploads and
# rendered clips both land here, so it needs room for a few clips at a time
# and it is not durable storage.
WORK_DIR=/tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not configurable, listed so it is not looked for
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# There is no API key, token or database. The captioning service is
# unauthenticated: it is the swappable infra behind the app's CaptioningProvider
# seam, and the app talks to it over a trusted network or not at all. Do not
# expose it to the internet as-is — put it behind whatever terminates TLS and
# authenticates for you.
#
# server/climax reads no configuration beyond WHISPER_MODEL. Everything else it
# does is a command-line flag; run `python main.py --help`.
